   },
   "prompt": "Identify any carbon atoms that change hybridization and the change in hybridization during the following reactions:<br>(a) 2-butene reacts with chlorine.<br>(b) benzene burns in air.",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "source",
    "solution": "CH<sub>3</sub><u>C</u>H = <u>C</u>HCH<sub>3</sub>(<em>sp</em><sup>2</sup>) + Cl $\\longrightarrow$ CH<sub>3</sub><u>C</u>H(Cl)H(Cl)CH<sub>3</sub>(<em>sp</em><sup>3</sup>); 2<u>C</u><sub>6</sub>H<sub>6</sub>(<em>sp</em><sup>2</sup>) + 15O<sub>2</sub> $\\longrightarrow$ 12<u>C</u>O<sub>2</sub>(<em>sp</em>) + 6H<sub>2</sub>O"
   }
  },
